IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 21 -- a corporation cannot be a member of its holding company, the exceptions and what a subsidiary must do about shares it holds.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- "holding company", "subsidiary", "wholly-owned subsidiary" and "nominee" are the keel's terms (ss 5, 5B: sg-groups.l4, which answers them from a list of control links).
-- This module asks each of them as a plain fact (BOOLEAN) named for the fact; it does not rebuild the links (NOTES.md, Seams).
-- Sections 76J, 76K, 76H and the others cited in subsections (4C), (6D), (6E) and (6G) are outside the sources; their effect is not coded, only what subsection 21 says of them.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".
-- Every exception is named in the text's own direction ("subsection (1) does not apply"): TRUE means the exception holds; `unless` or `but` met is `JUST FALSE`.
-- A failed "where" gate answers `JUST FALSE` on a duty and on a deeming; a failed "if" or "on application" on a grant answers `NOTHING` (NOTES.md, forks F-H-S1 and F-H-S3).
-- "within 14 days after" and "within the period of 12 months ... after" read the day of the event as in time (fork line F-H-P2); "6 months beginning with the day" is P10.

§ `Section 21(1) and (1A): the bar and the saving for book-entry securities`

-- src:3812 | 21.—(1) A corporation cannot be a member of a company which is
-- src:3813 | its holding company, and any allotment or transfer of shares in a
-- src:3814 | company to its subsidiary is void.
@ref s 21(1) (src:3812-3814)
GIVEN `the company is the holding company of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the corporation cannot be a member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is the holding company of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a corporation as "a member of a company which is its holding company"; the text says nothing of any other company

-- src:3812 | 21.—(1) A corporation cannot be a member of a company which is
-- src:3813 | its holding company, and any allotment or transfer of shares in a
-- src:3814 | company to its subsidiary is void.
@ref s 21(1) (src:3812-3814)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted or transferred in a company to its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the allotment or transfer of the shares is void` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted or transferred in a company to its subsidiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any allotment or transfer of shares in a company to its subsidiary is void"; the text says nothing of an allotment or transfer to anyone else

-- src:3816 | (1A) Subsection (1), insofar as it provides that any transfer of
-- src:3817 | shares in contravention of it is void, does not apply to a disposition of
-- src:3818 | book‑entry securities, but a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition
@ref s 21(1A) (src:3816-3818)
GIVEN `the transfer is a disposition of book-entry securities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1A) subsection (1) does not make the transfer void` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is a disposition of book-entry securities`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a disposition of book-entry securities"; the text says nothing here of any other transfer

-- "a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person, order the transfer": "on being satisfied" is a "when"; "on the application of" gates a grant.
-- src:3818 | book‑entry securities, but a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition
-- src:3819 | of book‑entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be
-- src:3820 | void may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person,
-- src:3821 | order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of
-- src:3822 | subsection (1).
@ref s 21(1A) (src:3818-3822)
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Registrar or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court is satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of subsection (1A) be void`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a Court, on being satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would in the absence of this subsection be void may ... order the transfer" (a failed "on being satisfied": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the application is made by the Registrar or any other person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court may order "on the application of the Registrar or any other person"; the text says nothing of an order without an application (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S3)

§ `Section 21(2) to (3): trustees, personal representatives and the 1967 members`

-- src:3826 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply where the subsidiary is concerned
-- src:3827 | as personal representative, or where it is concerned as trustee, unless
-- src:3828 | the holding company or a subsidiary thereof is beneficially interested
-- src:3829 | under the trust and is not so interested only by way of security for the
-- src:3830 | purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a
-- src:3831 | business which includes the lending of money.
@ref s 21(2) (src:3826-3831)
GIVEN `the subsidiary is concerned as personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary is concerned as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is so interested only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business which includes the lending of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` MEANS
    IF `the subsidiary is concerned as personal representative`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the subsidiary is concerned as trustee`
          THEN (IF `the holding company or a subsidiary of it is beneficially interested under the trust` AND (NOT `it is so interested only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business which includes the lending of money`)
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or where it is concerned as trustee, unless the holding company or a subsidiary thereof is beneficially interested under the trust and is not so interested only by way of security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business which includes the lending of money" (an "unless", met)
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for a subsidiary "concerned as personal representative" or "concerned as trustee"; the text says nothing of any other capacity

-- src:3833 | (3) This section does not prevent a subsidiary which, on
-- src:3834 | 29 December 1967, is a member of its holding company, from
-- src:3835 | continuing to be a member but, subject to subsection (2), the
@ref s 21(3) (src:3833-3835)
GIVEN `on 29 December 1967 the subsidiary is a member of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` MEANS
    IF `on 29 December 1967 the subsidiary is a member of its holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a subsidiary which, on 29 December 1967, is a member of its holding company"; the text says nothing of any other subsidiary

-- src:3835 | continuing to be a member but, subject to subsection (2), the
-- src:3836 | subsidiary has no right to vote at meetings of the holding company or
-- src:3837 | any class of members thereof.
@ref s 21(3) (src:3835-3837)
GIVEN `on 29 December 1967 the subsidiary is a member of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` MEANS
    IF (NOT `on 29 December 1967 the subsidiary is a member of its holding company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the vote is withheld from "a subsidiary which, on 29 December 1967, is a member of its holding company"; the text says nothing of any other subsidiary
    ELSE (IF `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (2)"; the text leaves a subsidiary within subsection (2) to that subsection
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the subsidiary has no right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members thereof" (a flat negative)

§ `Section 21(4) to (4C): a subsidiary that already holds shares when it becomes a subsidiary`

-- src:3839 | (4) This section does not prevent a subsidiary from continuing to be
-- src:3840 | a member of its holding company if, at the time when it becomes a
-- src:3841 | subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that
-- src:3842 | holding company, but —
@ref s 21(4) (src:3839-3842)
GIVEN `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` MEANS
    IF `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company"; the text says nothing of any other case (a failed "if" on an exception: fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:3847 | (a) subject to subsection (2), the subsidiary has no right to vote
-- src:3848 | at meetings of the holding company or any class of
-- src:3849 | members thereof; and
@ref s 21(4)(a) (src:3847-3849)
GIVEN `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` MEANS
    IF (NOT `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) belongs to the subsidiary that already holds shares when it becomes a subsidiary; the text says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (2)"; the text leaves a subsidiary within subsection (2) to that subsection
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the subsidiary has no right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members thereof" (a flat negative)

-- (4)(b): the duty applies unless (4A) takes it away ("ceases to apply if, during the period ..., the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company").
-- (4B) lets shares not disposed of be held subject to (4C) and (6E): fork line F-H-D4 in NOTES.md (the duty stands, and (4B) saves the holding).
-- src:3851 | (b) subject to subsections (4A) and (4B), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3852 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3853 | Court may allow after becoming the subsidiary of its
-- src:3854 | holding company, dispose of all of its shares in the holding
-- src:3855 | company.
@ref s 21(4)(b) (src:3851-3855)
GIVEN `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) belongs to the subsidiary that already holds shares when it becomes a subsidiary; the text says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply if, during the period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company" (subsection (4A))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- "within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the Court may allow after becoming the subsidiary": the last day is 12 months on, or the last day the Court allowed if later (P4).
-- src:3851 | (b) subject to subsections (4A) and (4B), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3852 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3853 | Court may allow after becoming the subsidiary of its
-- src:3854 | holding company, dispose of all of its shares in the holding
-- src:3855 | company.
@ref s 21(4)(b) (src:3851-3855)
GIVEN `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` 12 Months
    WHEN JUST allowed THEN
        IF allowed GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` 12 Months
        THEN allowed
        ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` 12 Months

-- src:3851 | (b) subject to subsections (4A) and (4B), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3852 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3853 | Court may allow after becoming the subsidiary of its
-- src:3854 | holding company, dispose of all of its shares in the holding
-- src:3855 | company.
@ref s 21(4)(b) (src:3851-3855)
GIVEN `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` MEANS
    IF `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company` AT LEAST `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` AND `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company` AT MOST `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` `the date the subsidiary became a subsidiary of its holding company` `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the Court may allow after becoming the subsidiary of its holding company, dispose of all of its shares" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:3859 | (4A) To avoid doubt, subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply if, during the
-- src:3860 | period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a
-- src:3861 | subsidiary of the holding company.
@ref s 21(4A) (src:3859-3861)
GIVEN `during the period referred to in subsection (4)(b), the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4A) subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply` MEANS
    IF `during the period referred to in subsection (4)(b), the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "ceases to apply if" names one case; the text says nothing of any other way for subsection (4)(b) to cease to apply

-- src:3865 | (4B) Any shares in the holding company that are not disposed of in
-- src:3866 | accordance with subsection (4)(b) may, subject to subsections (4C)
-- src:3867 | and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary.
@ref s 21(4B) (src:3865-3867)
GIVEN `the shares in the holding company are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections (4C) and (6E) are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4B) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares in the holding company are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)(b)` AND `subsections (4C) and (6E) are complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any shares in the holding company that are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)(b) may, subject to subsections (4C) and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary"; the text says nothing of any other shares, or of an exercise that is not "subject to" those subsections (fork line F-H-S3)

-- (4C)(a): "sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K apply with the necessary modifications, including the following modifications": an "including" list is open.
DECLARE `s 21(4C) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(4C)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares`
    `s 21(4C)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares`
    `s 21(4C)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied`
    `s 21(4C) another reference in sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K`

-- src:3871 | (4C) With respect to the shares referred to in subsection (4B) —
-- src:3873 | (a) subject to this subsection and subsection (6E),
-- src:3874 | sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K apply with
-- src:3875 | the necessary modifications, including the following
-- src:3876 | modifications:
-- src:3878 | (i) a reference to treasury shares is a reference to shares
-- src:3879 | referred to in subsection (4B);
-- src:3881 | (ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares is a
-- src:3882 | reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in
-- src:3883 | subsection (4B);
-- src:3885 | (iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to “as if they were
-- src:3886 | purchased by the company at the time they were
-- src:3887 | allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H
-- src:3888 | applied” is a reference to “as if they were already
-- src:3889 | held by the subsidiary at the time they were allotted,
-- src:3890 | in circumstances in which section 21(4) applied”;
-- src:3891 | and
@ref s 21(4C) (src:3871-3891)
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      reference IS A `s 21(4C) reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to the shares referred to in subsection (4B)"; the text says nothing of any other shares
    ELSE (CONSIDER reference
          WHEN `s 21(4C)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` THEN JUST "a reference to shares referred to in subsection (4B)"
          WHEN `s 21(4C)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares` THEN JUST "a reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in subsection (4B)"
          WHEN `s 21(4C)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied` THEN JUST "as if they were already held by the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(4) applied"
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "apply with the necessary modifications, including the following modifications"; the other necessary modifications are not stated

-- src:3896 | (b) the holding company must, within 14 days after any
-- src:3897 | change in the number of shares in the holding company
-- src:3898 | which are held by any of its subsidiaries under
-- src:3899 | subsection (4B), lodge with the Registrar a notice in the
-- src:3900 | prescribed form.
@ref s 21(4C) (src:3896-3900)
GIVEN `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (4B)` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (4B)` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (4B)` `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the holding company must, within 14 days after any change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (4B), lodge with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of the change is in time, fork line F-H-P2)

§ `Section 21(5) and (6): nominees and capitalisation of reserves`

DECLARE `s 21(5) subsection` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(5) subsection (1)`
    `s 21(5) subsection (3)`
    `s 21(5) subsection (4)`
    `s 21(5) subsection (4B)`
    `s 21(5) subsection (6A)`
    `s 21(5) subsection (6C)`
    `s 21(5) another subsection`

-- src:3904 | (5) Subject to subsection (2), subsections (1), (3), (4), (4B), (6A)
-- src:3905 | and (6C) apply in relation to a nominee for a corporation which is a
-- src:3906 | subsidiary as if references in those subsections to such a corporation
-- src:3907 | included references to a nominee for it.
@ref s 21(5) (src:3904-3907)
GIVEN subsection IS A `s 21(5) subsection`
      `the person is a nominee for a corporation which is a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is a nominee for a corporation which is a subsidiary`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsections apply "in relation to a nominee for a corporation which is a subsidiary"; the text says nothing of any other person
    ELSE (IF `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)"; the text leaves a subsidiary within subsection (2) to that subsection
          ELSE (CONSIDER subsection
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (4B)` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (6A)` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `s 21(5) subsection (6C)` THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names (1), (3), (4), (4B), (6A) and (6C) without saying "only"; the text says nothing of any other

-- src:3911 | (6) This section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares
-- src:3912 | in a holding company to a subsidiary which already lawfully holds
-- src:3913 | shares in the holding company if the allotment is made by way of
-- src:3914 | capitalisation of reserves of the holding company and is made to all
-- src:3915 | members of the holding company on a basis which is in direct
-- src:3916 | proportion to the number of shares held by each member in the
-- src:3917 | holding company.
@ref s 21(6) (src:3911-3917)
GIVEN `the subsidiary already lawfully holds shares in the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is made to all members of the holding company on a basis which is in direct proportion to the number of shares held by each member in the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` MEANS
    IF `the subsidiary already lawfully holds shares in the holding company` AND `the allotment is made by way of capitalisation of reserves of the holding company` AND `the allotment is made to all members of the holding company on a basis which is in direct proportion to the number of shares held by each member in the holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section does not prevent the allotment "if" it is by capitalisation of reserves and made to all members in direct proportion, to a subsidiary that already lawfully holds shares; the text says nothing of any other allotment (a failed "if" on an exception: fork line F-H-S3)

§ `Section 21(6A) to (6D): transfers by distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement`

DECLARE `s 21(6A) way of transfer` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(6A) a distribution in specie`
    `s 21(6A) an amalgamation`
    `s 21(6A) a scheme of arrangement`
    `s 21(6A) another way of transfer`

-- src:3919 | (6A) This section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares
-- src:3920 | in a holding company to a subsidiary by way of a distribution in
-- src:3921 | specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement but —
@ref s 21(6A) (src:3919-3921)
GIVEN way IS A `s 21(6A) way of transfer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 21(6A) a distribution in specie` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 21(6A) an amalgamation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 21(6A) a scheme of arrangement` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement"; the text does not say "only", and says nothing of any other way

-- src:3923 | (a) subject to subsection (2), the subsidiary has no right to vote
-- src:3924 | at meetings of the holding company or any class of
-- src:3925 | members thereof; and
@ref s 21(6A)(a) (src:3923-3925)
GIVEN `the shares were transferred to the subsidiary by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6A)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares were transferred to the subsidiary by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) belongs to a transfer by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement; the text says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (2)"; the text leaves a subsidiary within subsection (2) to that subsection
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the subsidiary has no right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members thereof" (a flat negative)

-- src:3927 | (b) subject to subsections (6B) and (6C), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3928 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3929 | Court may allow after the transfer to the subsidiary of the
-- src:3930 | shares in the holding company, dispose of all of the shares
-- src:3931 | in the holding company.
@ref s 21(6A)(b) (src:3927-3931)
GIVEN `the shares were transferred to the subsidiary by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares were transferred to the subsidiary by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) belongs to a transfer by way of a distribution in specie, amalgamation or scheme of arrangement; the text says nothing of any other
    ELSE (IF `during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply if, during the period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company" (subsection (6B))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:3927 | (b) subject to subsections (6B) and (6C), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3928 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3929 | Court may allow after the transfer to the subsidiary of the
-- src:3930 | shares in the holding company, dispose of all of the shares
-- src:3931 | in the holding company.
@ref s 21(6A)(b) (src:3927-3931)
GIVEN `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(6A)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` 12 Months
    WHEN JUST allowed THEN
        IF allowed GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` 12 Months
        THEN allowed
        ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` 12 Months

-- src:3927 | (b) subject to subsections (6B) and (6C), the subsidiary must,
-- src:3928 | within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the
-- src:3929 | Court may allow after the transfer to the subsidiary of the
-- src:3930 | shares in the holding company, dispose of all of the shares
-- src:3931 | in the holding company.
@ref s 21(6A)(b) (src:3927-3931)
GIVEN `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` MEANS
    IF `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company` AT LEAST `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` AND `the date the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company` AT MOST `s 21(6A)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares` `the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary` `the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if it allowed one`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period of 12 months or such longer period as the Court may allow after the transfer to the subsidiary of the shares in the holding company, dispose of all of the shares" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:3935 | (6B) To avoid doubt, subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply if, during
-- src:3936 | the period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a
-- src:3937 | subsidiary of the holding company.
@ref s 21(6B) (src:3935-3937)
GIVEN `during the period referred to in subsection (6A)(b), the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6B) subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply` MEANS
    IF `during the period referred to in subsection (6A)(b), the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "ceases to apply if" names one case; the text says nothing of any other way for subsection (6A)(b) to cease to apply

-- src:3944 | (6C) Any shares in the holding company that are not disposed of in
-- src:3945 | accordance with subsection (6A)(b) may, subject to subsections (6D)
-- src:3946 | and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary.
@ref s 21(6C) (src:3944-3946)
GIVEN `the shares in the holding company are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (6A)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections (6D) and (6E) are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6C) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares in the holding company are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (6A)(b)` AND `subsections (6D) and (6E) are complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any shares in the holding company that are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (6A)(b) may, subject to subsections (6D) and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary"; the text says nothing of any other shares, or of an exercise that is not "subject to" those subsections (fork line F-H-S3)

DECLARE `s 21(6D) reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(6D)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares`
    `s 21(6D)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares`
    `s 21(6D)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied`
    `s 21(6D) another reference in sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K`

-- src:3950 | (6D) With respect to the shares referred to in subsection (6C) —
-- src:3952 | (a) subject to this subsection and subsection (6E),
-- src:3953 | sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K apply with
-- src:3954 | the necessary modifications, including the following
-- src:3955 | modifications:
-- src:3957 | (i) a reference to treasury shares is a reference to shares
-- src:3958 | referred to in subsection (6C);
-- src:3960 | (ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares is a
-- src:3961 | reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in
-- src:3962 | subsection (6C);
-- src:3964 | (iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to “as if they were
-- src:3965 | purchased by the company at the time they were
-- src:3966 | allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H
-- src:3967 | applied” is a reference to “as if they were transferred
-- src:3968 | to the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in
-- src:3969 | circumstances in which section 21(6A) applied”; and
@ref s 21(6D) (src:3950-3969)
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (6C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      reference IS A `s 21(6D) reference`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (6C)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to the shares referred to in subsection (6C)"; the text says nothing of any other shares
    ELSE (CONSIDER reference
          WHEN `s 21(6D)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` THEN JUST "a reference to shares referred to in subsection (6C)"
          WHEN `s 21(6D)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares` THEN JUST "a reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in subsection (6C)"
          WHEN `s 21(6D)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied` THEN JUST "as if they were transferred to the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(6A) applied"
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "apply with the necessary modifications, including the following modifications"; the other necessary modifications are not stated

-- src:3971 | (b) the holding company must, within 14 days after any
-- src:3972 | change in the number of shares in the holding company
-- src:3973 | which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection
-- src:3974 | (6C), lodge with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed
-- src:3975 | form.
@ref s 21(6D) (src:3971-3975)
GIVEN `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (6C)` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6D)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` AT LEAST `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (6C)` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (6C)` `the date the notice in the prescribed form was lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the holding company must, within 14 days after any change in the number of shares in the holding company which are held by any of its subsidiaries under subsection (6C), lodge with the Registrar a notice in the prescribed form" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); the day of the change is in time, fork line F-H-P2)

§ `Section 21(6E) and (6F): the 10% limit and what follows from exceeding it`

-- (a): "must not at any time exceed 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company at that time". TRUE means the limit is exceeded. The text names no bearer, so there is no regulative rule (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path).
-- src:3979 | (6E) With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:3980 | (6C) —
-- src:3982 | (a) where the holding company has shares of only one class,
-- src:3983 | the aggregate number of shares held by all the subsidiaries
-- src:3984 | of the holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or
-- src:3985 | by the holding company as treasury shares, must not at any
-- src:3986 | time exceed 10% of the total number of shares of the
-- src:3987 | holding company at that time;
@ref s 21(6E)(a) (src:3979-3987)
GIVEN `the holding company has shares of only one class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate number of shares held by all the subsidiaries of the holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of shares of the holding company at that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(a) the aggregate number of shares exceeds 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the holding company has shares of only one class`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the holding company has shares of only one class, the aggregate number of shares held ... must not at any time exceed 10%" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); paragraph (b) governs a company with several classes)
    ELSE (IF `the aggregate number of shares held by all the subsidiaries of the holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares` * 100 GREATER THAN `the total number of shares of the holding company at that time` * 10
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not at any time exceed 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company at that time" (not exceeded)

-- src:3979 | (6E) With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:3980 | (6C) —
-- src:3992 | (b) where the share capital of the holding company is divided
-- src:3993 | into shares of different classes, the aggregate number of the
-- src:3994 | shares of any class held by all the subsidiaries of the
-- src:3995 | holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the
-- src:3996 | holding company as treasury shares, must not at any time
-- src:3997 | exceed 10% of the total number of the shares in that class
-- src:3998 | of the holding company at that time;
@ref s 21(6E)(b) (src:3979-3998)
GIVEN `the share capital of the holding company is divided into shares of different classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate number of the shares of the class held by all the subsidiaries of the holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of the shares in that class of the holding company at that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(b) the aggregate number of the shares of the class exceeds 10% of the total number of the shares in that class` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the share capital of the holding company is divided into shares of different classes`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the share capital of the holding company is divided into shares of different classes, the aggregate number of the shares of any class held ... must not at any time exceed 10%" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); paragraph (a) governs a company with one class)
    ELSE (IF `the aggregate number of the shares of the class held by all the subsidiaries of the holding company under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares` * 100 GREATER THAN `the total number of the shares in that class of the holding company at that time` * 10
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not at any time exceed 10% of the total number of the shares in that class of the holding company at that time" (not exceeded)

-- src:3979 | (6E) With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:3980 | (6C) —
-- src:4000 | (c) where paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened, the holding
-- src:4001 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or
-- src:4002 | procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary,
-- src:4003 | in accordance with section 76K before the end of the
-- src:4004 | period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that
-- src:4005 | contravention occurs, or such further period as the
-- src:4006 | Registrar may allow;
@ref s 21(6E)(c) (src:3979-4006)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(c) the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) where paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened, the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares" (a duty whose "where" gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- "before the end of the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further period as the Registrar may allow": P10 (the day counts as day 1).
-- src:4000 | (c) where paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened, the holding
-- src:4001 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or
-- src:4002 | procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary,
-- src:4003 | in accordance with section 76K before the end of the
-- src:4004 | period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that
-- src:4005 | contravention occurs, or such further period as the
-- src:4006 | Registrar may allow;
@ref s 21(6E)(c) (src:4000-4006)
GIVEN `the day on which the contravention occurs` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the further period the Registrar allowed, if the Registrar allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the further period the Registrar allowed, if the Registrar allowed one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months
    WHEN JUST allowed THEN
        IF allowed GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months
        THEN allowed
        ELSE `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day on which the contravention occurs` 6 Months

-- src:4000 | (c) where paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened, the holding
-- src:4001 | company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or
-- src:4002 | procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary,
-- src:4003 | in accordance with section 76K before the end of the
-- src:4004 | period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that
-- src:4005 | contravention occurs, or such further period as the
-- src:4006 | Registrar may allow;
@ref s 21(6E)(c) (src:4000-4006)
GIVEN `the day on which the contravention occurs` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the further period the Registrar allowed, if the Registrar allowed one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled` IS A DATE
      `the disposal or cancellation was in accordance with section 76K` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled` AT LEAST `the day on which the contravention occurs` AND `the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled` AT MOST `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` `the day on which the contravention occurs` `the last day of the further period the Registrar allowed, if the Registrar allowed one` AND `the disposal or cancellation was in accordance with section 76K`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary, in accordance with section 76K before the end of the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that contravention occurs, or such further period as the Registrar may allow" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); "before the end of the period" is read as up to and including its last day)

-- (d) and (e): TRUE means a dividend or other distribution may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares.
-- src:3979 | (6E) With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:3980 | (6C) —
-- src:4008 | (d) where the subsidiary is a wholly‑owned subsidiary of the
-- src:4009 | holding company, no dividend may be paid, and no other
-- src:4010 | distribution (whether in cash or otherwise) of the holding
-- src:4011 | company’s assets (including any distribution of assets to
-- src:4012 | members on a winding up) may be made, to the subsidiary
-- src:4013 | in respect of the shares referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:4014 | (6C); and
@ref s 21(6E)(d) (src:3979-4014)
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(d) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)"; the text says nothing of any other share
    ELSE (IF `the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company, no dividend may be paid, and no other distribution (whether in cash or otherwise) of the holding company's assets (including any distribution of assets to members on a winding up) may be made, to the subsidiary in respect of the shares referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)" (a flat negative)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (d) speaks of a wholly-owned subsidiary; paragraph (e) speaks of one that is not, and is the question for that case

-- src:3979 | (6E) With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:3980 | (6C) —
-- src:4016 | (e) where the subsidiary is not a wholly‑owned subsidiary of
-- src:4017 | the holding company, a dividend may be paid and other
-- src:4018 | distribution (whether in cash or otherwise) of the holding
-- src:4019 | company’s assets (including any distribution of assets to
-- src:4020 | members on a winding up) may be made, to the subsidiary
-- src:4021 | in respect of the shares referred to in subsection (4B) or
-- src:4022 | (6C).
@ref s 21(6E)(e) (src:3979-4022)
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(6E)(e) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares are shares referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With respect to any share referred to in subsection (4B) or (6C)"; the text says nothing of any other share
    ELSE (IF (NOT `the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) where the subsidiary is not a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company, a dividend may be paid" (a failed "where" on a "may": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1; paragraph (d) says no for a wholly-owned subsidiary)

-- (6F): "excess shares" means such number of the shares ... as resulted in the limit referred to in subsection (6E)(a) or (b) being exceeded.
-- The limit is 10% of the total, so the shares allowed are the whole number of shares up to a tenth of the total (rounded down), and the excess is what is held above that.
-- src:4026 | (6F) In subsection (6E)(c), “excess shares” means such number of
-- src:4027 | the shares, held by any subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by
-- src:4028 | the holding company as treasury shares at the time in question, as
-- src:4029 | resulted in the limit referred to in subsection (6E)(a) or (b) being
-- src:4030 | exceeded.
@ref s 21(6F) (src:4026-4030)
GIVEN `the aggregate number of shares held by any subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares at the time in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of shares (or of the shares of the class) of the holding company at that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate number of shares held by any subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares at the time in question` * 100 GREATER THAN `the total number of shares (or of the shares of the class) of the holding company at that time` * 10
    THEN `the aggregate number of shares held by any subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C) or by the holding company as treasury shares at the time in question` - FLOOR (`the total number of shares (or of the shares of the class) of the holding company at that time` * 10 / 100)
    ELSE 0

